21 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ff601f0c-4e57-5018-96f0-7310734b6270" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496223 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496223 #edb/ref 1069 "q-178524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496223 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496223 #edb/ref 1071 "$6\\le {3}^{2}$ **and** $6$ is even, **and** $13$ is a prime number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:6\\le {3}^{2}$\n\n- $Q:6\\text{ is even}$\n\n- $R:13\\text{ is a prime number}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496223 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "02eac488-c624-58c9-8e5f-2f3e12e226ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496223 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $6\\le {3}^{2}$ and $6$ is even. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{6\\le {3}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{6\\text{ is even}}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧Q.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $13$ is a prime number. This corresponds to $R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{6\\le {3}^{2}\\text{ and }6\\text{ is even }}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∧\\,Q},\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{13\\text{ is a prime number}}_{⏟}}_{R}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(P∧Q)∧R.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496234 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496234 #edb/ref 1069 "q-170736" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496234 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496234 #edb/ref 1071 "Express the statement \"$8$ is a natural number and divisible by $4$\" in symbolic form, where $P=$ \"$8$ is a natural number\" and $Q=$ \"$8$ is divisible by $4.$\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496234 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "20409d3d-4f9a-55b3-ae07-39d336721810" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496234 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧.$\"\n\nNote that the given sentence is a shortened version of the following full sentence:\n\n$8$ is a natural number and $8$ is divisible by $4.$\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{8\\text{ is a natural number}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{8\\text{ is divisible by }4}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∧Q.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496236 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496170 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496236 #edb/ref 1069 "q-177454" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496236 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496236 #edb/ref 1071 "$7$ is a composite number **and** odd, **or** $2+6\\ge 10.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $A:7\\text{ is a composite number}$\n\n- $B:7\\text{ is odd}$\n\n- $C:2+6\\ge 10$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496236 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2491e070-37d1-586f-b67e-4103f90ed72e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496236 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $7$ is a composite number and odd. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{7\\text{ is a composite number}}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{7\\text{ is odd}}_{⏟}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∧B.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $2+6\\ge 10.$ This corresponds to $C.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{7\\text{ is a composite number}\\text{ and }\\text{odd}}_{⏟}}_{A\\,∧\\,B},\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{2+6\\ge 10}_{⏟}}_{C}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(A∧B)∨C.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496262 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496262 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496171 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496262 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496262 #edb/ref 1069 "q-178160" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496262 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496262 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{{\\{1,2\\}\\cup \\{3\\}=\\{1,2,3\\}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{0\\in Z}}\\,\\overset{∧}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{and}}}\\,\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{1\\text{ is positive}}}}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∧\\,R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $Q∧R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $P∧(Q∧R)$ is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496262 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5f1de2e0-3e98-599c-9d88-57f6ce468e91" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496262 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is true. Therefore, $Q∧R$ is true, and the result is true:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P∧(Q∧R) & ≡\\text{true}∧\\overset{\\text{true}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{true}∧\\text{true})}} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{true} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496270 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496150 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496270 #edb/ref 1069 "q-178520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496270 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496270 #edb/ref 1071 "$9$ is a perfect square, **or** $3\\ge 4$ **or** $3=5-1.$\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $P:9\\text{ is a perfect square}$\n\n- $Q:3\\ge 4$\n\n- $R:3=5-1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496270 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6a09aec4-5239-540b-baf9-5ce099cfcf55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496270 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $9$ is a perfect square. This corresponds to $P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $3\\ge 4$ or $3=5-1.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{3\\ge 4}_{⏟}}_{Q}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3=5-1}_{⏟}}_{R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $Q∨R.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{9\\text{ is a perfect square}}_{⏟}}_{P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{3\\ge 4\\text{ or }3=5-1}_{⏟}}_{Q\\,∨\\,R},\n$$\n\nthat is, $P∨(Q∨R).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496272 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496272 #edb/ref 1069 "q-177457" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496272 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496272 #edb/ref 1071 "$4$ is even **or** ${4}^{2}=12$, **and** $-2$ is an integer number.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $M:4\\text{ is even}$\n\n- $N:{4}^{2}=12$\n\n- $P:-2\\text{ is an integer number}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496272 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "717ad532-4709-5a63-b627-09752527f241" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496272 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $4$ is even or ${4}^{2}=12.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ is even }}_{⏟}}_{M}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{{4}^{2}=12}_{⏟}}_{N},\n$$\n\nthat is, $M∨N.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $-2$ is an integer number. This corresponds to $P.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{4\\text{ is even}\\text{ or }{4}^{2}=12}_{⏟}}_{M\\,∨\\,N},\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{-2\\text{ is an integer number}}_{⏟}}_{P}\n$$\n\nthat is, $(M∨N)∧P.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496275 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496160 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496275 #edb/ref 1069 "q-177717" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496275 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496275 #edb/ref 1071 "$6|10$ **and** $6|18,$ **or** $11$ is prime **and** odd.\n\nExpress the compound statement above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $M:6|10$\n\n- $P:6|18$\n\n- $N:11\\text{ is prime}$\n\n- $Q:11\\text{ is odd}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496275 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7d328347-cdbe-5da0-b048-5a26fc979b28" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496275 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$∧$\", while the word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts:\n\n- **Part 1:** $6|10$ and $6|18.$ This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{6|10}_{⏟}}_{M}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{6|18}_{⏟}}_{P}\n$$\n\nthat is, $M∧P.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $11$ is prime and odd. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{11\\text{ is prime}}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{11\\text{ is odd }}_{⏟}}_{Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∧Q.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{6|10\\text{ and }6|18}_{⏟}}_{M\\,∧\\,P}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{11\\text{ is prime }\\text{and}\\text{ odd }}_{⏟}}_{N\\,∧\\,Q},\n$$\n\nthat is, $(M∧P)∨(N∧Q).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496281 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496281 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496151 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496281 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496281 #edb/ref 1069 "q-177355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496281 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496281 #edb/ref 1071 "$2+3$ equals $5$ **or** $\\pi $ is rational.\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $A:2+3\\text{ equals }5$\n\n- $B:\\pi \\text{ is rational}$\n\nExpressed in symbolic form, our statement can be written as\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496281 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86cefea1-4583-5e59-84d3-54626f201af0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496281 #edb/ref 1074 "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{2+3\\text{ equals }5}_{⏟}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{\\pi \\text{ is rational}}_{⏟}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A∨B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496303 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496303 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496303 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496185 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496303 #edb/ref 1069 "q-175930" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496303 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496303 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{{\\overset{P}{\\overset{⏞}{\\{1,2\\}\\cup \\{2\\}=\\{1,2\\}}}\\,\\overset{∨}{\\overset{⏞}{\\text{or}}}\\,\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{11\\text{ is prime}}}}_{⏟}}_{P\\,∨\\,Q}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{⏟}}_{∧}\\,{{2\\text{ is a perfect square}}_{⏟}}_{R}\n$$\n\nFor the compound statement above, we have that\n\n$\\,$ $P∨Q$ is {{field-1}},\n$\\,$ $R$ is {{field-2}},\n$\\,$ $(P∨Q)∧R$ is {{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496303 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bbfbaab7-10b5-57a8-a26d-3c15f79b1087" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496303 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's recall the following facts about the \"and\" $(∧)$ and \"or\" $(∨)$ logical connectives:\n\n- The statement $A∧B$ is true if *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\n- The statement $A∨B$ is true if either $A$ is true, or $B$ is true, or *both* $A$ and $B$ are true.\n\nIn our case, $P$ is true, $Q$ is true, and $R$ is false. Therefore, $P∨Q$ is true, but the result is false:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(P∨Q)∧R & ≡\\overset{\\text{true}}{\\overset{⏞}{(\\text{true}∨\\text{true})}}∧\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{true}∧\\text{false} \\\\  & ≡\\text{false}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496309 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496120 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496309 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496309 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186496174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186496309 #ed